    "ps2": "src/shdPersona.c shdPersonaSetupChannels0x0011aaa0, lines2194..2253: ten start/current snapshots; selector0/1 uses work open/close duration;2/3 fixed4;4/5 alternate open/close duration; each20-byte row supplies x/y,alpha, two float timing factors to36-byte channel state. Six table addresses fixed by actual switch arms.",
    "steam": "ordinary .shared0x41f0d0..0x41f598: same ten current->start snapshots,36-byte channel stride, selected table and same five row fields/duration scaling. Seven-way jump table0x41f57c has ordered destinations41f276,41f28a,41f29e,41f2a7,41f2b0,41f2c4,41f2d8. Branch targets/materialized bases establish semantic selector identity, not candidate byte similarity.",
    "switch": "0x71002a93b0..0x71002a9710: same snapshots and seven-arm selector, exact table bases/duration rules independently recovered from instructions.0x71002a9550 LDP s1,s2,[x8,#12];0x71002a9554 FMUL and0x71002a9568 FMUL establish raw float timing loads, not integer numeric conversion implied by the untyped decompiler display. Only work duration uses SCVTF.",
    "work_destination": "Golden first channel at0x460, stride36: start x/y+0/+4, target x/y+8/+12, current x/y+16/+20, startAlpha+24,targetAlpha+25,currentAlpha+26, duration+28,delay+32. Do not overwrite a PS2 parent-work allocation with this Golden parent layout.",
    "other_ps2_consumers": [
      "shdPersonaTaskInit0x001175e0 initializes current x/y/alpha from old selector1 close bank",
      "shdPersonaTweenComparison0x0011c3e0 resets current/start/target x/y/alpha from old selector0 open bank after comparison; also zeroes channel duration/delay"
    ],
    "other_steam_consumers": [
      "ordinary .shared0x41bc20..0x41c164 includes initialization reads within actual close bank0xb168a0 (not candidate0xb16a80)",
      "ordinary .shared0x420740..0x420e14 includes reset reads from open bank0xb16ca0"
